course: dictionary
lesson: 2949
title: Drink: a word that works two ways
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word drink can be an action or a thing. As a verb it means to take a liquid into your mouth and swallow it. «On a sunny day a honeybee lands on a flower, drinks sweet nectar with its long tongue and flies off» shows the action: the bee is swallowing the nectar.
explain: As a noun, a drink is something you drink, or an amount of it. «A hot drink can still scald a small child badly fifteen minutes after it was made.» Here drink is a thing, not an action. Try the swap test: «A hot swallow» makes no sense, so drink must be a noun.
explain: Drink also appears in sums and science. A bottle that holds 500 millilitres, with 150 drunk, has 500 minus 150 left. Plants drink water through their roots, and the body needs water to work well.
explain: Safety comes first. Drink water when you play sport, and never drink from bottles you do not know.
fact: Drink can be a verb (drink, drinks, drank, drunk, drinking) or a noun (a drink, drinks).
fact: To drink is to take water, milk, juice or another liquid into your mouth and swallow it.
fact: A drink is something you drink, or an amount of it.
fact: For grown-ups, «to drink» can mean to drink alcohol, and «Drinking and driving is against the law and dangerous.»
fact: «Butterflies drink nectar, fruit juice and water through a long proboscis that uncurls like a party blower.»
exercise: What is drink in «A hot drink can still scald a small child badly fifteen minutes after it was made»? | To swallow water quickly | *A thing you drink | To wash your hands | A bottle that is empty
exercise: A bottle holds 500 millilitres. Ben drinks 150 millilitres at lunch. How many millilitres are left? | *350 | 650 | 200 | 150
exercise: What is the safest thing to do with a drink from a bottle you do not know? | *Do not drink it, and tell a grown-up | Share it with your friends | Drink it quickly to be polite | Drink half and keep the rest
test: Which word completes this? Yesterday the honeybee ___ sweet nectar from the flower. | drinks | drunk | *drank | drinking
test: In «Plants drink water through their roots», what does drink mean? | Play in the water | Pour water onto the soil | *Take water in and absorb it | Spill water on the floor
exam: Which sentence uses drink as a noun, meaning a thing you drink? | «We drank water all day.» | *«The cold drink was lovely and fizzy.» | «Please drink slowly, Sam.» | «He will drink his juice now.»
